/// <remarks>
/// <see href="https://streams.spec.whatwg.org/#dictdef-underlyingsink">Streams Standard: 5.2.3 The underlying sink API</see>
/// </remarks>
/// <param name="Start">A function that is called when a new chunk of data is ready to be written to the underlying sink. The stream implementation guarantees that this function will be called only after previous writes have succeeded, and never before start() has succeeded or after close() or abort() have been called. <see href="https://streams.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-underlyingsink-start">Streams Standard: 5.2.3 The underlying sink API</see></param>
