/// <summary>
/// The AudioNode interface is a generic interface for representing an audio processing module. Examples include: an audio source (e.g., an HTML &lt;audio&gt; or &lt;video&gt; element, an OscillatorNode, etc.), the audio destination, intermediate processing module (e.g., a filter like BiquadFilterNode or ConvolverNode), or volume control (like GainNode) Note: An AudioNode can be target of events, therefore it implements the EventTarget interface.
/// </summary>
/// <remarks>
